    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-056 — CSS `background:` URL forms.** Three commits. **Docs follow after merge.**\n\nCloses the last 4 of 11 Wikipedia `background:` forms. **Reaches 11/11 form coverage** for the first time since ADR-045.\n\n## The verified delta (screenshot 2026-11-01)\n\nRan against Wikipedia HTML article:\n\n| Icon | Before ADR-056 | After ADR-056 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Search magnifier** (top bar) | invisible | **renders** (10px high — translateY caveat) |\n| **External link icons** (body) | invisible | **renders** |\n| **Wikipedia logo** (`<img>`, not background) | renders | renders unchanged — Commit 1 split held |\n| **Article body/layout** | correct | correct — zero regression |\n\n**This is a real production delta on Wikipedia.** First time since ADR-045 that visual rendering changed materially.\n\n## Three commits (isolated for safety)\n\n### Commit 1 — Infrastructure (no behavior change, 2e9bff5)\n\n- 5 new `LayoutBox` fields mirroring ADR-047 mask: `background_size_w/h`, `background_pos_x/y`, `background_no_repeat`\n- 3 new `layout_element` reads (mirror mask block)\n- **`paint_image` split into `paint_img_element` + `paint_background_image`** — this is the split that could regress `<img>` rendering\n- **Checkpoint**: all 658 tests pass unchanged\n\n### Commit 2 — Grammar parser (visible delta, a0e2c0e)\n\n- Replaces `try_expand_background`'s 3 early-return lines with token classifier + assembler\n- Handles `[color || image || repeat || position [/ size]]*` order-free per CSS spec\n- 5 helper functions: `is_color_token`, `is_repeat_token`, `is_position_token`, `is_url_token`, `is_length_token`\n- `bg_detail::classify` + `bg_detail::BgTokens` for token accumulation\n- **This is where Wikipedia icons start rendering**\n- 1 test flipped (ADR-055's `url() forms dropped entirely` → `now expand to 3 longhands`), 5 new tests\n\n### Commit 3 — Fixture + README (10f1eb2)\n\n- `docs/adr056-background-url-test.html` — 5-row permanent fixture, self-contained via inline `data:image/svg+xml` URLs\n- Each row exercises one Wikipedia form\n- README fixture list updated\n\n## What's now handled\n\n```\nbackground: <color>                                  (ADR-055)\nbackground: none                                     (ADR-055)\nbackground: url(x)                                   ADR-056\nbackground: url(x) no-repeat right                   ADR-056 (Wikipedia form 3)\nbackground: url(x) 100% 50% no-repeat                ADR-056 (Wikipedia form 4)\nbackground: #fff url(x) repeat                       ADR-056\nbackground: no-repeat center / 1.23em url(x)         ADR-056 (Wikipedia form 2)\nbackground: #f8f9fa url(x) no-repeat center          ADR-056\n```\n\n11/11 `background:` forms from Wikipedia CSS parse correctly.\n\n## Regression protections applied\n\n- **`paint_image` → `paint_img_element` rename is a direct copy** — ADR-034 `<img>` tests unaffected\n- **`paint_background_image` is a new function** — no existing path routes to it\n- **`try_expand_background`'s gradient/comma early-returns preserved** — ADR-055's tests still pass\n- **`background: none` early-return preserved** — ADR-055's behavior intact\n- **`ctx` scope relocation** — first attempt put new reads at line 336, before `LengthContext ctx` at line 434. Caught immediately, relocated to line 558.\n\n## The magnifier caveat (documented)\n\n`.cdx-text-input__start-icon` renders at correct size, **~10px too high**. Needs `translateY(-50%)`, which alone would move it to `y=-3` without `top: 50%`, which needs `parent_content_height` threading.\n\nFull chain:\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `background-image` renders | ✅ ADR-056 (this PR) |\n| `translateY(-50%)` | ⏸ deferred on `parent_content_height` |\n| `top: 50%` | ⏸ same blocker |\n\nAfter ADR-056 the icon is visible. After the `parent_content_height` cycle, it'll be perfectly centered.\n\n## Wikipedia forms still dropped entirely\n\n- `background: linear-gradient(...)` — 1 form, no gradient support anywhere\n- `background: url(a), url(b)` — multi-layer, rare\n\n## Test count\n\n- 658 → 663 cases (+5)\n- 2514 → 2550 assertions (+36)\n- All existing tests pass unchanged except ADR-055's url-form test (flipped per ADR-056 grammar)\n\n## Deferred (documented in ADR-056)\n\n- `translateY()` / `top: 50%` (blocked on `parent_content_height`)\n- Percentage `background-size` (needs element dims in parser)\n- `cover` / `contain` (needs paint-time aspect math)\n- `repeat-x` / `repeat-y` / `space` / `round` (variants beyond `repeat` / `no-repeat`)\n- Multi-layer backgrounds\n- `linear-gradient` / `radial-gradient`\n- `background-clip` / `background-origin`\n\nRefs #249\n",
